            <ArticleTitle>[An uncommon cause of acute abdomen--hemorrhage into an accessory hepatic lobe].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>253-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The author presents the case-history of a young female who was hospitalized because suspicion of acute abdomen. The condition did not call for an urgent operation, during the subsequent examination a hepatoma was suspected. On operation a congenital accessory liver lobe was found, the size of a fist, and was removed. The cause of manifestations of acute abdomen was haemorrhage into its parenchyma.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
